  "final_url": "https://townofsavoy.com/town-clerk/",
  "title": "Town Clerk - Town Of Savoy | Town Of Savoy",
  "text": "Town Clerk - Town Of Savoy | Town Of Savoy\nPlease ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of\nwebsite accessibility\nSkip to main content\nNO DATA\nNavigate to\nHome\nNavigate to\nGovernment\nAgendas & Minutes\nAnnual Reports\nCalendar\nElection Information\nFee Schedule\nForms & Permits\nNews & Notices\nPublic Records Request\nTown Documents\nVeterans Services\nNavigate to\nDirectory\nTown Committees\nSavoy School Committee\nTown Boards\nTown Departments\nNavigate to\nCommunity\nEmployment & Volunteer Opportunities\nFrequently Asked Questions\nLinks\nSchool\nSubscribe to Updates\nNavigate to\nContact Us\nTown Clerk\nValerie Reiner\nTown Clerk\nPhone: (413) 743-4290 x 1006\nEmail:\ntownclerk@townofsavoy.com\nOffice Hours:\nTuesday 11:00 AM - 1:00 PM; or by appointment\nMassachusetts State Midterm Election is November 3rd\n2026 State Election Warrant\nAll mail-in ballots were mailed on 10/05 for the applications I currently have.  Mail-in applications will still be accepted until 10/27.\nIn Person Early Voting Dates for the Midterm Election are:\nSunday, October 18:  10am - 2pm\nTuesday, October 20:  11am-1pm & 5pm to 7pm\nSaturday, October 24:  9am-11am & 3pm-5pm\nTuesday, October 27:  11am-1pm & 5pm-7pm\nVoting is at the Town Hall\nLast Day to Register for the Midterm:\nSaturday, October 24 at 5pm\nLast Day to Request a mail-in ballot for the Midterm:\nTuesday, October 27 at 5pm\nBallots must be postmarked by\nNovember 3rd\nto be counted.  If you are mailing the ballot on November 3rd, go into the post office and have them hand stamp/cancel it.  Otherwise, it may not get a November 3rd postmark.\nA number of ballots were received after the primary election in September.  I would suggest, if at all possible, drop off your Mail-in ballot at the Town Hall during business hours, or in the Town Clerk drop box on the front porch.\nIn Person Voting Hours on November 3rd are 7am-8pm at the Town Hall\n2026 Vote By Mail Instructions\nMassachusetts Voters Information Booklet-Audio Version\n2026 Census Notice\nAll Savoy Residences will soon be receiving the annual street listing/census by mail.  Per Massachusetts state law (Massachusetts General Laws, Ch. 51, Sec. 4), these must be returned to the Town Clerk by January 31, 2026.\nFailure to return the street listing/census will result in all voters at the residence being designated as inactive, which can then lead to removal from the voter rolls.\nIf you do not receive a street listing/census please contact me at 413-743-4290 ext. 1006 or at\ntownclerk@townofsavoy.com\n.\nThe completed street listings/census may be returned in person at the Town Office during office hours, in the \"Town Clerk\" lockbox on the porch of the Town Offices, or send by mail to:\nTown Clerk\n720 Main Road\nSavoy, MA  01256\nTown Clerk Posted: June 18, 2026\n180 Residents in Savoy will be receiving a letter shortly telling them that they are now designated as inactive voters due to a failure to return their Annual Street Listing, as required by law.  These voters who are thus designated will be required to show an ID and fill out a residence form before they can vote in a town meeting or any election.  Returning the signed postcard enclosed in the letter will make the voter active again.\nValerie Reiner\nSavoy Town Clerk\nDocuments\nDog License Information\nRequest for Savoy Records\nTown Election Information\n2026 State Primary Election Warrant\n2026 State Primary Results for Savoy\nTown Information\nAddress: 720 Main Rd,\nSavoy, MA, 01256\nPhone: (413) 743-4290\nEmail:\nsbadmin@townofsavoy.com\nOffice Hours\nMonday - Friday 9:00 AM - 1:00 PM;\nOffice Closed Wednesday\n© 2026 Designed & Hosted by\nTown Web\n|\nAccessibility\n|\nPrivacy Policy",
